  "rationale": "This inscription is a catalogue of the Athenian ephebes for the year of the archon Philotimos (late 2nd century AD). It lists the primary officials of the ephebeia, including the kosmetes Marcus Aurelius Zenon of Marathon, followed by the sophronistai and a monthly schedule of gymnasiarchs. The roster of ephebes is organized by their respective tribes (Ptolemais, Akamantis, Hadrianis, Oineis, Kekropis, Hippothontis). The text is fragmentary, with several lacunae in the names and month names.",
